    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nUnified `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. Verified against the audit output: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` (region) + `27` (FY of 2026\u201109\u201103) + `16E6609E` (HASH8) + `1` (Luhn CHK).\n\nChanges, each kept small and in a low-complexity class:\n\n- **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 `service()` now builds the full memberId: `region + 2\u2011digit FY + hash8 + CheckDigit.checkDigit(base)`. Reuses the existing `hash8`/`blank` helpers (same SHA\u2011256-over-(telephone+lastName) first\u20118\u2011hex as before, so it matches the region-and-hash identity the test recomputes).\n- **`CheckDigit.java`** \u2014 Luhn now takes a `String` (the `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` base) instead of reading `customerCode` off the owner; kept referenced (no dead code) as the CHK source.\n- **`Locality.java`** \u2014 `locality()` simplified to `region(owner)` (the region is now the memberId prefix, no dash to parse). This keeps `OwnerSegment` correctly referencing the memberId's region with no edit to that class.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 dropped the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings, added `memberId` (from the stored value); `customerCode` auto-map disappears with the DTO field.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** / **`AuditOwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 both audit records now emit `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` schema blocks with a single `memberId`, and removed `checkDigit`, regenerating `OwnerDto` accordingly.\n\nKept structural impact low: the entity's internal `customerCode` storage column is reused as the memberId slot, so the large `Owner` class, the DB schema, the pipeline YAML, and `DeduplicateCustomerCode` (collision handling now naturally applies to the memberId) were left untouched. `fiscalYear` stays derived from the registration date, consistent with the FY segment now embedded in the memberId.",
